{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442357080,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDQxMDM3NDA3Nw=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442384004,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDY0MDExOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/210#issuecomment-140640119"},"message":"+100\n\nI don't want to craft anything within Python that figures out how/where to install stuff outside Python's scope. But it is trivial to grab the generated completions and put then where they belong in the Debian packaging (or an RPM for that matter). So: yes to generate, no to Python-based install.\n\nLooks like you have a patch. Is that all it needs?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442413343,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc1NjIwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/210#issuecomment-140756205"},"message":"starcluster (btw -- they apparently have similar to our system, just no \"Python API\" generation, but with shortcut aliases for commands etc), and  uses similar (which inspired this one) module -- optcomplete  (for optparse) but that one doesn't require any \"global\" enabling shim, so startcluster's completion setup for a user is just a single tiny file to source...\nso I guess we just need a closer look into this beast on how to make it easier to \"deploy\" for the user, but indeed probably is the way to go and indeed those 2 lines changes is enough to start but then Python code should provide additional goodies may be even linked into Constraints system","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442413473,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc1NjgwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/210#issuecomment-